cff-version: 1.2.0
title: EU Building Heat Model
message: If you use this model, please cite it and the associated article.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Alsulaiman
    given-names: Abdurahman
    affiliation: Oxford Institute for Energy Studies, Oxford, UK
  - family-names: Alajwad
    given-names: Ali
    affiliation: RENEW Lab, Johns Hopkins University, Baltimore, MD, USA
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/alajwadha/EU-Building-Heat-Model
abstract: >-
  A NUTS3-resolution techno-economic model of residential heat across the EU-27,
  the United Kingdom and Switzerland to 2050. It screens hydrogen against
  heat-pump electrification on annual levelised cost, on cold-snap dispatch in
  buildings, district heat and power, and on whether a peaker that wins the
  dispatch can recover its capital.
keywords:
  - building heat decarbonisation
  - hydrogen
  - heat pumps
  - capacity adequacy
  - techno-economic assessment
